The Nomla Authors
=================

"The Nomla Authors" in the copyright notices of this repository are:

    Felix Becker

Upstream authors
----------------

Nomla is a port of Mumla and contains code derived from the following
projects. Their authors keep their copyright; the notices in the individual
files name them, and those notices are preserved in every derived file.

  Mumla (https://gitlab.com/quite/mumla), 2020-2026
      Daniel Lublin and the Mumla contributors.
      Mumla is a fork and continuation of Plumble.

  Humla (https://gitlab.com/quite/humla), 2020-2026
      Daniel Lublin and the Humla contributors.
      Humla, the Mumble protocol library of Mumla, is a fork of Jumble.

  Plumble (https://github.com/acomminos/Plumble), 2013-2017
  Jumble (https://github.com/acomminos/Jumble), 2013-2017
      Andrew Comminos <andrew@comminos.com> and the Plumble and Jumble
      contributors.

Further copyright holders named in the notices of derived files:

  Allan Nordhøy (2022)
  Bartkk0 (2022)
  Nicolas Peugnet <n.peugnet@free.fr> (2024)
  William Goodspeed (2026)

The translations carried over from Mumla were contributed by many translators
through Weblate (https://hosted.weblate.org/engage/mumla/); the git history
records their names.

Third-party libraries bundled with Nomla have their own authors and licenses;
see NOTICE and NOTICE.md.
